Changes made by DMD61 to the original HDRDisplayCalibrate code:
- Guided sensor dialogs in the HDR wizard and in Verify & report.
- The ArgyllCMS bundled next to the exe is always used first; the bin folder is read-only when it is bundled.
- Italian translation of the interface.
- HDR wizard: opens on HDR or SDR calibration according to the monitor and switches Windows HDR on/off by itself;
  "Before you start" box; numbered steps in the profile prompt; final profile name; closing window; report export to
  PDF or HTML saved automatically; HDR colour check (24 colours, dE2000); work folder emptied at the end.
- Version 0.1.0 of DMD TV Calibrate: new program name, executable (DMDTVCalibrate.exe), icon, and its own settings
  and documents folders (DMDTVCalibrate), so it can be installed side by side with HDRDisplayCalibrate.
